  "notes": [
    "Brewing Temperature & Time: Steep with near-boiling water between 195°F and 205°F (90°C–96°C) for 3 to 4 minutes.",
    "Recommended Ratio: Use 1 to 2 teaspoons (approximately 3 to 4 grams) of loose leaf per 8 ounces (240 ml) of fresh water.",
    "Multiple Steeps: High-quality whole-leaf Yunnan black tea can be re-infused 3 to 5 times, adding 30 to 60 seconds to each subsequent steep.",
    "Flavor Profile: Known traditionally in China as *Dianhong*, it produces a rich amber-red liquor with naturally sweet notes of malt, honey, and subtle cocoa.",
    "How It Compares: Grown from Yunnan’s large-leaf tea trees (*Camellia sinensis* var. *assamica*), it delivers the rich body of a classic breakfast tea but with significantly softer tannins and lower astringency."
